<Gooey xmlns="wonderforge.io/gooey/2026">
  <!-- The right-hand pane of beat 2.5, on its own so it can be rebuilt
       without disturbing anything else.

       When vim writes counter.gooey, the running pane has to come back
       from disk — and the obvious way to do that, re-patching the whole
       Stage, also destroys the Terminal next to it: the guest is killed
       and vim reopens, losing the cursor, the undo history and whatever
       the presenter was halfway through typing. Live is the smallest
       subtree that contains the Include and not the editor.

       Keep this identical to the fragment in NARRATION.md beat 2.5. It
       is a second copy of four lines, which is the price of being able
       to rebuild them; the file they resolve to has no second copy at
       all, which is the point the slide is making. -->
  <VStack Name="Live" Grid.Col="1">
    <Counter Label="…and that file, running"
             Count="{{.Count}}"
             Bump="{{.Bump}}"/>
  </VStack>
</Gooey>
